# Leave unset in normal deployments: the app calls a same-origin /api, which the Vite dev server
# and server.cjs both proxy to the backend. Set this only when the API lives on a different host.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api

# Where /api is proxied to (dev server and server.cjs). Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:5000.
# API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5000

# REQUIRED to build for deployment: the Shopify app's PUBLIC client id (Partner Dashboard → the app →
# Client credentials). It goes into the page for Shopify App Bridge, which uses it to tell Shopify
# which app is loading. Public by design — it is in the address bar of every Shopify redirect — and
# NOT the client secret, which must never appear in the frontend. `npm run build` stops without it,
# because a build with a wrong or missing key opens as a blank page inside the Shopify admin.
#
# Set it in the shell that runs the build (the app has one id per environment), e.g. in PowerShell:
#   $env:VITE_SHOPIFY_API_KEY = "your-client-id"; npm run build
# or put it in frontend/.env.local, which git ignores.
# VITE_SHOPIFY_API_KEY=
